241    -- GET /admin/principals/
242    ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
243    -- The listing endpoint any roles screen needs, absent until now
244    -- (ui-authorisation-design-v1.md section 5). Framework surface: it is identity, which
245    -- spec-patch-06 rule 1 assigns to road-kit, so it lives in road_admin_api beside the rest.
246    --
247    -- Static segment, declared BEFORE principals/:principal_id/roles/ for readability only -- ORDS
248    -- resolves static segments ahead of templates regardless of declaration order.
249    --
250    -- NOTE on the "query" parameter name: this repeats the deviation documented at length on
251    -- GET /events/search/. ORDS reserves "q" globally for its AutoREST JSON filter syntax and returns
252    -- a platform-level 400 for any non-JSON value, even on a plain PL/SQL-source handler. The
253    -- external parameter is therefore "query"; road_admin_api's own JSON contract still uses "q", and
254    -- the mapping is contained here at the ORDS layer.
255    --
256    -- offset/limit keep their spec-mandated external names (ords-api-design-standards-v1.md section
257    -- 6.1). ORDS reserves BOTH for pagination and validates them as numeric before dispatching, so a
258    -- ?limit=abc never reaches this block: it comes back as ORDS's own 400, with ORDS's envelope
259    -- ("code":"BadRequest") rather than error_api's. Verified against dev 2026-08-19 -- the same
260    -- class of platform behaviour as the reserved "q" above, found the same way.
261    --
262    -- DEFAULT NULL ON CONVERSION ERROR therefore cannot fire for these two today. It stays because it
263    -- is right for any bind ORDS does not pre-validate and because relying on an undocumented
264    -- platform guard is how a 500 arrives later; but do not read it as live cover. The behaviour that
265    -- IS live is pinned by test/endpoint/admin-principals.endpoint.sh.
266    ords.define_template(
267      p_module_name => 'hello_api.admin',
268      p_pattern     => 'principals/',
269      p_comments    => 'Principal directory'
