SQL> 
SQL> -- The demo application's API (spec-patch-08 section 6).
SQL> --
SQL> -- Registered by deploy/create/97_demo.sql, NOT by deploy/create/90_rest.sql -- an adopter
SQL> -- deploying the framework does not get these routes.
SQL> --
SQL> -- Every handler follows the framework's two-line preamble: establish session context, or 401.
SQL> -- ORDS exposes no schema-callable pre-dispatch hook, so this is per handler by necessity
SQL> -- (spec-patch-06 section 6.3) and bin/check-handler-coverage.sh is what stops one being forgotten.
SQL> --
SQL> -- The handlers are thin. They bind path and query parameters and the body into one JSON payload
SQL> -- and call demo_todo_api, which enforces the permission requirement ITSELF -- so authorisation
SQL> -- travels with the operation rather than living only in the handler. An adopter copying this demo
SQL> -- should copy that arrangement and throw the domain away.
SQL> --
SQL> -- "query" not "q": ORDS reserves q globally for its AutoREST JSON filter syntax and returns a
SQL> -- platform-level 400 for any non-JSON value, even on a plain PL/SQL-source handler. Same
SQL> -- deviation, same reason, as GET /admin/principals/ and road-cal's GET /events/search/.
