SQL> -- The scope the ORDS privilege above requires must be one the scaffold actually mints, or every
SQL> -- request to /todos/* is a 401 before any PL/SQL runs.
SQL> --
SQL> -- Appended HERE rather than added to deploy/create/80_standalone.sql.tmpl, deliberately: rule 1 of
SQL> -- spec patch 08 is that the demo may never cause a framework change, and the scaffold's issued
SQL> -- scope list is framework surface. This is also what a real adopter has to do, so the demo
SQL> -- demonstrating it is the point rather than a workaround.
SQL> --
SQL> -- ORDER MATTERS: 80_standalone.sql rewrites scope_name wholesale on every deploy, so this append
SQL> -- must run after it -- 97_ > 80_ -- and must re-apply each time. Idempotent by construction.
SQL> update jwt_scaffold_config
  2     set scope_name = scope_name || ' todo.rw',
  3         updated_at = systimestamp
  4   where config_id = 1
  5     and scope_name not like '%todo.rw%';

